      "## Build trust before they call",
      "Homeowners are letting you into their house and trusting you with an expensive job. Your site needs to earn that before the first conversation.",
      "### Real photos of real work",
      "Stock photos of smiling models in hard hats are easy to spot and do nothing for trust. Photos of your actual team, your trucks and your finished jobs, ideally before-and-after shots, do far more. They don't need to be professional. A clean, well-lit phone photo of a finished basement beats a polished stock image every time.",
      "### Reviews in context",
      "Show a few specific reviews on the pages they relate to: a furnace review on your furnace page, a bathroom review on your bathroom page. Link to your Google reviews so visitors can see the full picture. Our post on [why Google reviews matter](/blog/google-reviews-and-ai-search) covers how to earn more of them.",
      "### Credentials that matter in Ontario",
      "Show the licences, registrations and coverage that apply to your trade, such as an Electrical Safety Authority (ESA) licence for electrical contractors, TSSA certification for gas work, WSIB coverage, and liability insurance. List any warranties you offer in plain language. These details reassure careful homeowners and separate you from operators who can't show them.",
      "### A human face",
      "An About page with the owner's photo and a few sentences about how you work goes a long way. People hire people.",
      "## One page per service",
      "A single 'Services' page with a bulleted list doesn't help anyone. Give each main service its own page that explains what's included, common signs a homeowner needs it, roughly how long it takes, what affects the price, and answers to the questions you hear on every estimate.",
      "These pages convert better because they match exactly what the visitor searched for, and they help you rank on Google and get cited by AI assistants for those specific services.",
      "## Service area pages done right",
      "If you serve several GTA cities, pages for your main areas can help, but only if each one is genuinely useful. Talk about the jobs you've actually done there, local housing stock, common issues, and reviews from customers in that city. Copying one page and swapping the city name creates thin pages that Google treats as spam. See our [local SEO guide](/blog/local-seo-guide) for more.",
      "## Speed and mobile performance",
      "A slow website loses visitors before they see anything. Google's Core Web Vitals give useful targets: the main content should load within about 2.5 seconds, the page should respond quickly when tapped, and the layout shouldn't jump around while it loads. Large uncompressed photos are the most common culprit on contractor sites. Our post on [website speed](/blog/website-speed-costs-customers) goes deeper.",
      "![A tradesperson reviewing a fast-loading website on a phone inside a work van](/blog/img/website-that-converts-2.webp \"A fast, simple mobile site keeps homeowners from hitting the back button.\")",
      "## Write like you talk to customers",
      "Skip the corporate language. Write the way you'd explain things at the kitchen table: clear, specific, and honest about what affects price and timing. Answer the questions people actually ask, like 'Do I need to replace my whole AC or just the coil?', and you'll build trust while helping your search rankings at the same time.",
      "## Measure what matters",
      "Pretty traffic graphs don't pay the bills. Track the things that do:",
      "- Calls from the website, ideally with call tracking.",
      "- Form submissions and chats.",
      "- Estimates booked and jobs won from website leads.",
      "If you know a site brought in 30 leads last month and 12 became jobs, you can make real decisions about where to spend.",
      "## A quick checklist",
      "- Clear service, area and phone number on the first screen.",
      "- Click-to-call and a short form on every page.",
      "- Real photos of your work and team.",
      "- Specific reviews near the services they mention.",
      "- Licences, insurance and warranties clearly listed.",
      "- A page for each main service.",
      "- Fast loading on a phone.",
      "- Every lead acknowledged within minutes.",
      "## The bottom line",
