      "- **Your own phone:** turn off Wi-Fi and load your homepage and a service page on mobile data. Time it. How long until you can see what you do and tap your phone number?",
      "## Understanding Core Web Vitals",
      "Google measures loading experience with three Core Web Vitals. Here's what each means in plain English:",
      "- **Largest Contentful Paint (LCP):** how long until the main content, usually the big headline or hero image, appears. Good is 2.5 seconds or less.",
      "- **Interaction to Next Paint (INP):** how quickly the page responds when someone taps a button or menu. Good is 200 milliseconds or less.",
      "- **Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS):** how much the page jumps around while loading, like a button moving just as you tap it. Good is 0.1 or less.",
      "## The fixes that make the biggest difference",
      "### 1. Shrink your images",
      "On contractor websites, oversized photos are the number one cause of slow pages. A photo straight off a modern phone can be several megabytes. Resize images to the size they actually display, use modern formats like WebP, and let images further down the page load only when needed. This alone often cuts load time dramatically.",
      "### 2. Lose the heavy extras",
      "Autoplay video backgrounds, image sliders, animation libraries and a dozen tracking scripts all slow pages down. Ask whether each one actually helps a homeowner decide to call you. Usually the answer is no.",
